  "result": "Perfect! All 124 tests pass. I've successfully implemented VAT (Value Added Tax) calculations for the invoicing system:\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **src/invoices.js** \u2014 Added VAT calculation:\n   - Created `lineVat()` helper to calculate VAT on the amount after discount\n   - VAT is calculated as: (lineTotal - lineDiscount) \u00d7 vatRate / 100\n   - VAT is rounded per line using `roundCents` and clamped at 0\n   - Updated `invoiceTotals()` to return `{ subtotal, discount, vat, total }`\n   - Formula: `total = subtotal - discount + vat`\n\n2. **src/render.js** \u2014 Updated to display VAT:\n   - Shows \"Subtotal\" line when discount > 0 OR vat > 0\n   - Shows \"Discount\" line when discount > 0\n   - Shows \"VAT\" line when vat > 0\n   - VAT appears just above the Total line\n\n3. **Tests added** \u2014 17 new tests:\n   - 10 VAT tests in invoices test (calculation, rounding, multiple lines, formula verification)\n   - 7 VAT render tests (display, formatting, positioning, edge cases)\n\n4. **Existing tests updated** \u2014 Adapted to include VAT in calculations and output verification\n\nThe system now properly computes VAT per line based on the amount after discount, rounds each line's VAT independently, and displays the total VAT on the invoice.",
